\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2b</p></td><td><p>Clip</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.870.645.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015391.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[512,127,0,"<p>1. Fit the engine components drive belt pulley (1a) and fix it tightening\nthe bolts (1b) to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>CRANKSHAFT PULLEY</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.1 - 2.6</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Fit the single drive belt.</p><p>2. Rotate the fixed tensioner (2a) for the engine components drive\nbelt using the tool (2a) until the tools (1c) comes out, then tighten\nthe cam tensioner bolt (2d) to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2b</p></td><td><p>Key</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.968.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2c</p></td><td><p>Clip</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.870.645.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>C